<%= render "shared/page_header",
      title: "Where Elephants Live",
      intro: "Elephants live in Africa and Asia. Wherever they live, they need three things: lots of plants to eat, " \
             "water every day and plenty of space to walk. The place where an animal lives is called its habitat." %>

<div class="section">
  <h2>Where in the world?</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-icon" aria-hidden="true">🌍</div>
      <h3>Africa</h3>
      <p>
        There are two kinds of African elephants. Savanna elephants live on wide, grassy plains in more than 20 countries,
        like Kenya, Tanzania and Botswana. Forest elephants live in thick rainforests in countries like Gabon and Cameroon.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-icon" aria-hidden="true">🌏</div>
      <h3>Asia</h3>
      <p>
        Asian elephants live in forests and grasslands in 13 countries, like India, Sri Lanka and Thailand, and on the
        islands of Sumatra and Borneo. More than half of all wild Asian elephants live in India.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figure class="photo-block">
    <%= render "shared/image_placeholder", label: "Map coming soon" %>
    <figcaption>A map of where elephants live today.</figcaption>
  </figure>
</div>

<div class="section">
  <h2>Underground or up a tree?</h2>
  <ul class="fact-list">
    <li>
      <span class="fact-label">Underground?</span>
      <span class="fact-value">
        No! Elephants don't live in holes. But they do dig. They use their feet, trunks and tusks to dig for water in dry
        riverbeds, and to dig up salty soil to eat.
      </span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="fact-label">Up a tree?</span>
      <span class="fact-value">
        No way! Elephants are far too heavy to climb. But trees are still useful. Elephants eat the leaves, rest in the
        shade and scratch their backs on the bark. Sometimes they push a tree over to reach the tasty leaves at the top.
      </span>
    </li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="section">
  <h2>What do elephants need?</h2>
  <ul class="fact-list">
    <li>
      <span class="fact-label"><span aria-hidden="true">💧</span> Water every day</span>
      <span class="fact-value">Elephants drink, splash and roll in mud every day, so they stay close to rivers, lakes and water holes.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="fact-label"><span aria-hidden="true">🌿</span> Lots of plants</span>
      <span class="fact-value">A grown-up elephant eats more than 100 kg of plants a day. That's heavier than a grown-up person!</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="fact-label"><span aria-hidden="true">🌳</span> Shade</span>
      <span class="fact-value">Trees give shade, which helps elephants stay cool on hot days.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="fact-label"><span aria-hidden="true">🚶</span> Space to walk</span>
      <span class="fact-value">Elephant families walk a long way to find food and water as the seasons change. They often use the same paths every year.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="fact-label"><span aria-hidden="true">🧂</span> Salt</span>
      <span class="fact-value">Elephants lick salty rocks and eat salty soil. This gives them minerals that plants don't have.</span>
    </li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="section">
  <h2>Do elephants have a home?</h2>
  <div class="info-block">
    <p>
      Elephants don't build nests or dens. Instead, each family has a big area it knows really well, called a
      <em>home range</em>. The family walks around it all year. Where there's lots of food and water, a home range can be
      smaller than a big city. In dry deserts, it can be as big as a small country!
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="highlight-box">
    <p>
      <strong>Did you know?</strong> Each elephant family is led by a grandma elephant called the <em>matriarch</em>.
      When it hasn't rained for a long time, she remembers where to find water. Her family depends on her!
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="section">
  <h2>More habitat facts</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Lots of places</h3>
      <p>Elephants live on grassy plains, in rainforests and swamps, on mountains and even in deserts.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Nature's helpers</h3>
      <p>Elephants knock down trees, dig water holes and spread seeds in their dung (poo). This helps lots of other animals and plants.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Less room</h3>
      <p>People are building farms and towns where elephants used to live. Losing their space is one of the biggest dangers elephants face.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
